DET-003
        |
        v
MITRE ATT&CK
T1059.001 — PowerShell
```

DET-003 provides behavioral visibility into one execution characteristic associated with PowerShell.

---

# Telemetry Sources

## Sysmon Event ID 1

Primary detection source:

```text
Process Creation
```

Useful information includes:

```text
Image
CommandLine
ParentImage
User
ProcessId
ParentProcessId
Computer
Timestamp
```

---

## PowerShell Event ID 4104

Supporting telemetry:

```text
Script Block Logging
```

This telemetry can provide visibility into PowerShell script content and can help an analyst understand what occurred after a suspicious process execution is identified.

---

## Sysmon Event ID 3

Supporting network telemetry:

```text
Network Connection
```

This can help determine whether suspicious PowerShell execution was associated with outbound or lateral network activity.

---

# Telemetry Correlation

```text
                 PowerShell Execution
                         |
          +--------------+--------------+
