```

Multiple telemetry sources provide greater context than a single event.

---

# DET-003 Detection

Detection:

```text
DET-003 — Encoded PowerShell Execution
```

Primary SPL:

```spl
index=* EventCode=1
(CommandLine="*-EncodedCommand*" OR CommandLine="* -enc *")
```

Portfolio output:

```spl
index=* EventCode=1
(CommandLine="*-EncodedCommand*" OR CommandLine="* -enc *")
| eval detection="DET-003 - Encoded PowerShell Execution"
| table _time detection host User Image CommandLine
```

---

# Detection Workflow

```text
Process Creation
      |
      v
PowerShell?
      |
      v
Inspect CommandLine
      |
      v
Encoded Argument?
    /        \
   NO        YES
   |          |
   v          v
Normal     DET-003
Review        |
              v
        T1059.001 Context
              |
              v
        Analyst Triage
```

---

# Controlled Validation

A benign PowerShell payload was used:

```powershell
$cmd='Write-Output "DET003 Positive Validation"'
```

The command was encoded:

```powershell
$encoded=[Convert]::ToBase64String([Text.Encoding]::Unicode.GetBytes($cmd))
```

and executed:

```powershell
powershell.exe -EncodedCommand $encoded
```

The command only produced text output.

Its purpose was to safely reproduce the execution characteristic targeted by DET-003.

---

# Positive Test

```text
powershell.exe
      |
      v
-EncodedCommand
      |
      v
Sysmon Event 1
      |
      v
Splunk
      |
      v
DET-003
      |
      v
TRIGGER
```

**Result:** PASS

---

# Negative Test

Normal PowerShell commands were executed:

```powershell
Get-Date
```

and:

```powershell
Get-ComputerInfo | Select-Object WindowsProductName
```

These did not contain encoded-command arguments.

```text
Normal PowerShell
       |
       v
No Encoded Argument
       |
       v
DET-003
       |
       v
NO TRIGGER
```

**Result:** PASS

